 "_bluefin_scope_comment": "v13 BlueFin policy: Blue whale D call and Fin whale downsweep come ONLY from Gerlache, SOI and Elephant Island (ElephantIsland2013Aural/2014); Kerguelen 2005/2014/2015 are used for every class they annotate EXCEPT Blue whale D call and Fin whale downsweep (their annotations there are dropped, and those classes are masked, not trained as negatives); every other BlueFin site-year is ignored entirely (split: ignore).",
 "_bluefin_comment": "BlueFin library: only LF call types are annotated, and only the ones with a selection table per site-year (convert_bluefin_library.py SITES; e.g. no Minke whale at casey2014/casey2017/ElephantIsland2014/Greenwich64S2015/kerguelen2014/RossSea2014). Everything not listed is MASKED there, incl. all HF classes (the band-limited audio still carries LF energy of humpback/seals, so unannotated != absent). To use BlueFin as pure negatives for an HF class again, add that class to annotated_classes.",
 "_sources_comment": "Keys are glob patterns matched (first match wins) against the source name = stem rule result or the audio folder name. annotated_classes: 'all' or a list = classes this source was actually annotated for; every other class is MASKED (no loss, no metric) for its files. split: random | train_only | val_only. val_only_classes: a file containing any annotation of these classes is forced into validation (and those annotations never reach training). sample_weight: multiplier on how often this source's windows are drawn.",
